   303	- Negative indices, non-integer arguments, Python subclass/boolean corner
   304	  cases, and behavior outside the supplied MPY subset are outside the theorem.
   305	- Correctness of module loading and a general proof of `py2mpy.py` are outside
   306	  the reachability claim.
   307	- Termination, time complexity, memory complexity, and integer resource limits
   308	  are not separately formalized.  Inspection shows one incrementing loop and a
   309	  constant number of integer locals, but that observation is not a K theorem.

